Agreed, with one flag on the example — it's more informative than it looks.

The sample changed content, not just register. Baseline: execute the strategy according to plan. Adjusted: move quickly and adapt as we go. Those are opposite commitments. If the sample varies meaning while demonstrating magnitude, the user can't tell whether they're ratifying a voice or a strategy, and any correction they make is ambiguous between the two. Rule for the schema: comparative samples hold propositional content fixed and vary only register. Same claim, two voices. Otherwise the mechanism you just assigned to magnitude ratification can't do the job.

The adjusted line is also two firewall hits. Triadic parallel construction, and "move fast, learn fast" is stock startup register. That's useful — it shows the firewall has to run against the readback's own samples, not only the final artifact. A sample that trips the firewall misrepresents what will actually ship. Worth stating as a check: samples are subject to the same firewall as output.

And it's arguably more than one legible step, which makes it a good calibration case for what "one step" means in practice. Worth keeping in the spec as a worked example of overshoot.

Terminology — agreed, two riders. Alternatives should appear only on low-confidence flagged items; enumerating B and C for every assumption rebuilds the review queue by another route. And the closing line needs to be mode-aware — "if unchanged, Mimic proceeds using A" is true under /fast and false under /slow, where nothing proceeds without ratification.

Always-compile-internally — right call. One consequence worth naming: if the spec layer always exists, it's the natural place for the firewall and the mechanic checks to run, before generation rather than as a post-hoc review of prose. The user-facing distinction is delivery only — spec artifact or deliverable — which is a cleaner framing than treating them as two modes of operation.

That's it from me on architecture. Firewall list next: per domain, structural entries included, each rendered as a failing check, and now with the additional requirement that it applies to readback samples too.
